# SCHOOL INCURSIONS

SUNSHINE COAST - BRISBANE - MELBOURNE - SYDNEY - ADELAIDE - PERTH

#### SCHOOL DRUMMING INCURSIONS – Bring the energy of African drumming and dance to your school!

Rhythm Culture's Drum Sing Dance school incursions are packed with exciting rhythmic activities that will have your students on the edge of their seats! Through the power of traditional West African rhythms, students connect through music, movement and sound in a lively, hands-on experience that gets everyone involved.

From exploring coordination, connection and musical dynamics to discovering tempo and rhythm through the incredible sound of the djembe, students are immersed in an energetic and interactive musical experience. These workshops are fast-paced, engaging, educational and, above all, great fun!

#### Interactive School Drumming & Dance Workshops for All Ages

Our school drumming incursions are designed for primary and secondary students, with every student having the opportunity to play their own real African drum. Combining drumming, singing and dance, our school cultural workshops are active, dynamic and educational, bringing energy, culture, rhythm and confidence into the classroom or school hall.

With programs suited to different age groups and year levels, our professional artists adapt each workshop to engage students and create an experience that is both enjoyable and age-appropriate. Students get active, learn something new and experience the physical and emotional benefits of participating in music and dance.

#### Experience the Culture Behind the Rhythms

What makes Rhythm Culture's school drumming incursions particularly special is the cultural knowledge and experience our artists bring to each workshop. All our drumming facilitators have studied in West Africa and share their personal stories, musical knowledge and experiences of Africa's wonderful and diverse cultural traditions.

Students don't just learn to play a drum or follow a dance movement; they get to experience something of the culture, history and traditions behind the music.

Get ready for an unforgettable school experience filled with rhythm, movement, culture, connection and plenty of fun!

No extra fees for drum hire. All students will have access to a West African drum at no extra cost.

Experience Rhythm Culture artists all over Australia with no extra travel costs.

All Rhythm Culture artists have studied and been trained in Africa. 

Every student willl play a full sized African drum. Quality authentic instruments that are comfortable to play and easy to get a good sound.

